Stages: SDD

Purpose:
  Formal registry of all engineering stages used by the SDLC and STLC.
  A stage is a named engineering responsibility with defined inputs,
  outputs, and gate criteria. Stages are the building blocks of chains
  (bax chains/chains.sdd -> Stages, DefaultFlow).

  This file is the authoritative stage list — chains/chains.sdd ->
  Stages is a summary copy for chain context, not the registry itself.


Owns:
  ./

Scope:
  Stage definitions
  Stage purposes
  Stage inputs/outputs
  Stage ownership
  Stage activation conditions


DoesNotOwn:
  Project-specific flows (bax project/flows.sdd)
  Project-specific chains (bax chains/chains.sdd)
  Engineering skills (bax skills/)
  Task instances (bax tasks/)
  Project architecture (bax project/architecture.sdd)


Stages:

  Business delivery stages — the business-to-engineering bridge of the
  delivery chain DL1 (Phase 151):

    BC:     Business Case
      Purpose: Understand the business problem, goal, scope and context.
      Owner:    HUMAN (business) + AR support
      Input:    user prompt/project brief, context
      Output:   business case artifact (problem, goal, scope, context)
      Activates: at the start of every delivery chain — the first step
    BR:     Business Requirement
      Purpose: Define what the business requires from the system.
      Owner:    HUMAN (business) + AR support
      Input:    business case artifact
      Output:   requirement artifact (business requirements list)
      Activates: after BC, before BD
    BD:     Business Design
      Purpose: Define the business-level solution/design.
      Owner:    AR
      Input:   requirement artifact
      Output:   business design artifact (solution shape at business level)
      Activates: after BR, before DS
    DS:     Decision
      Purpose: Record and finalize important decisions derived from the
               requirements/design. Runtime = decision ledger DEC-XXX
               records (proposed -> review -> approved).
      Owner:    HUMAN gate + ORCHESTRATOR
      Input:    business design artifact, requirements
      Output:   decision ledger entries (DEC-XXX.sdd)
      Activates: after BD, before TK
    TK:     Task
      Purpose: Break the approved work into actionable technical tasks.
               Runtime = task engine (tasks/INDEX.sdd entries with
               depends/state/priority).
      Owner:    ORCHESTRATOR
      Input:    approved decisions
      Output:   task breakdown (tasks/INDEX.sdd entries)
      Activates: after DS, before BDD

  Orchestration stages — analysis/decision points that begin or redirect
  a chain:

    AN:     Analysis
      Purpose:  Initial scope, requirement, and constraint analysis.
      Owner:    AR
      Input:    prompt, decision, finding
      Output:   analysis document, scope definition
      Activates: when new work is initiated or existing work is impacted

    AR:     Architecture
      Purpose:  Architecture decisions, boundary drawing, modularity.
      Owner:    AR
      Input:    analysis document, project model
      Output:   architecture decision, module boundaries
      Activates: when new feature requires architecture decisions or
                 existing architecture is impacted

    IMPACT: Impact Analysis
      Purpose:  Determine what a bug or change actually affects before
                touching it.
      Owner:    AR
      Input:    bug report, change request, affected components
      Output:   impact scope, affected stages
      Activates: when existing work is modified (bugfix, change, hotfix)

  Engineering discipline stages — reusable branch stages. Every
  implementation branch follows the same unified pipeline:

      XX -> CR-XX -> RF-XX -> XX-TS -> SC-XX
      (XX = DB, BE, API, FE, MD, DC)

    BDD:    Behavior-Driven Development
      Purpose:  Define acceptance criteria in Given/When/Then format.
                Bridge between requirements and implementation.
      Owner:    QA
      Input:    requirements, analysis
      Output:   BDD scenarios, acceptance criteria
      Activates: when requirements need formal acceptance criteria

    DB:     Database
      Purpose:  Schema, data, and migration changes.
      Owner:    DB
      Input:    requirements, architecture
      Output:   schema, migrations, seed data
      Activates: when data model changes are required

    BE:     Backend
      Purpose:  Backend service and business-logic implementation.
      Owner:    BE
      Input:    requirements, BDD, DB schema
      Output:   backend code, API endpoints
      Activates: when backend implementation is required

    API:    API / Contract
      Purpose:  API contract, integration, and compatibility.
      Owner:    API
      Input:    requirements, backend implementation
      Output:   API contract, integration tests
      Activates: when API surface changes or integration is required

    FE:     Frontend
      Purpose:  Web frontend implementation.
      Owner:    FE
      Input:    requirements, API contract
      Output:   frontend code, UI components
      Activates: when UI changes are required

    MD:     Mobile
      Purpose:  Mobile application implementation.
      Owner:    MD
      Input:    requirements, API contract
      Output:   mobile code, platform-specific components
      Activates: when mobile changes are required

    DC:     Documentation
      Purpose: Create/update technical and project documentation (formal
               stage; the D1 chain arm remains the runtime execution arm).
      Owner:    D1/DOCS
      Input:    implementation, decisions, task context
      Output:   documentation artifacts (docs/, technical docs)
      Activates: during the delivery branches, after implementations

    CR:     Code Review (scoped — see CRScopedSemantics)
      Purpose:  Peer review of branch implementation before merge.
      Owner:    AR
      Input:    implementation, decision, task context
      Output:   review report, approval, change requests
      Activates: after XX implementation, before RF-XX

    RF:     Refactor (scoped — see RFScopedSemantics)
      Purpose:  Restructure/clean branch implementation per CR findings,
                prior to final test validation.
      Owner:    relevant discipline owner (BE/DB/API/FE/MD/DC)
      Input:    review report, change requests (from CR-XX)
      Output:   refactored implementation
      Activates: after CR-XX raises change requests (skipped if CR-XX
                 passes clean), before XX-TS

    ARCH:   Architecture Verification
      Purpose:  Verify that implementation conforms to architecture
                decisions and principles.
      Owner:    AR
      Input:    implementation, architecture decision
      Output:   architecture review, compliance report
      Activates: after BE/API/FE/MD implementation, before QA

    DB_TS:  Database Test Suite
      Purpose:  Database migration, integrity, and data tests.
      Owner:    QA
      Input:    database implementation
      Output:   test report, coverage metrics
      Activates: after RF-DB (or CR-DB if clean), before SC-DB

    BE_TS:  Backend Test Suite
      Purpose:  Backend unit, integration, and contract tests.
      Owner:    QA
      Input:    backend implementation
      Output:   test report, coverage metrics
      Activates: after RF-BE (or CR-BE if clean), before SC-BE

    FE_TS:  Frontend Test Suite
      Purpose:  Frontend component, integration, and E2E tests.
      Owner:    QA
      Input:    frontend implementation
      Output:   test report, coverage metrics
      Activates: after RF-FE (or CR-FE if clean), before SC-FE

    MD_TS:  Mobile Test Suite
      Purpose: Mobile platform, integration, and offline tests.
      Owner: QA
      Input: mobile implementation
      Output: test report, coverage metrics
      Activates: after RF-MD (or CR-MD if clean), before SC-MD

    DC_TS:  Documentation Tests / Validation
      Purpose: Validate documentation against the actual implementation
                (docs match code reality — no drift).
      Owner:    QA
      Input:    documentation artifacts, implementation
      Output:   documentation validation report
      Activates: after RF-DC (or CR-DC if clean), before SC-DC

      (API-TS has no dedicated stage — it maps to BE_TS scoped to API
      contracts; see step-keys.sdd [SK4].)

    SC:     Security (scoped — see SCScopedSemantics)
      Purpose:  Security validation of a single branch's output, run
                immediately after that branch's own tests pass — not a
                whole-system gate.
      Owner:    SC
      Input:    branch implementation, XX-TS results, threat model
      Output:   security findings, remediation tasks
      Activates: after XX-TS passes, before that branch is marked
                 complete

    QA:     Quality Assurance
      Purpose:  Aggregate testing and quality validation across all
                branches once each branch's own XX-TS/SC-XX has passed.
      Owner:    QA
      Input:    all branch XX-TS/SC-XX results
      Output:   test results, quality report
      Activates: after all required branches' XX-TS/SC-XX pass, before DO

    DO:     DevOps
      Purpose:  Build, deployment, infrastructure validation.
      Owner:    DO
      Input:    implementation, QA results
      Output:   deployment, infrastructure config
      Activates: after QA passes, before VR

    VR:     Verification
      Purpose:  Final system verification and acceptance.
      Owner:    VR
      Input:    all stage outputs, test results
      Output:   verification report, acceptance decision
      Activates: after all required stages complete — VR is the final
                 stage of any chain (bax chains/chains.sdd -> Important)

    BRU:    Business Requirement Unit
      Purpose:  Validate implementation against business requirements.
      Owner:    HUMAN
      Input:    implementation, business requirements
      Output:   business acceptance decision
      Activates: after all branch CR-XX pass, before manual check

    CRU:    Code Requirement Unit
      Purpose:  Validate implementation against code requirements and standards.
      Owner:    QA
      Input:    implementation, code standards, architecture decisions
      Output:   code quality report, compliance decision
      Activates: after BRU passes, before manual check


  CRScopedSemantics (Phase 151):
    definition: CR is ONE stage. CR-DB, CR-BE, CR-API, CR-FE, CR-MD,
      CR-DC are the SAME stage executed with a `scope:` parameter naming
      the branch artifact under review.
    rule: scoped CR instances are NOT separate stages — no stage
      explosion; each instance reviews its branch output against that
      branch's requirements, design and BDD.
    rule: a delivery branch is complete only when its scoped CR has
      passed (see step-keys.sdd [SK3]).
    notation: in chains and traces, write CR{scope=BE} etc.; the short
      key form CR-BE is the dictionary alias (bax workflow/step-keys.sdd).

  RFScopedSemantics (Phase 151):
    definition: RF is ONE stage. RF-DB, RF-BE, RF-API, RF-FE, RF-MD,
      RF-DC are the SAME stage executed with a `scope:` parameter naming
      the branch artifact under refactor.
    rule: scoped RF instances are NOT separate stages — no stage
      explosion.
    rule: RF-XX runs after its CR-XX raises change requests; if CR-XX
      passes clean, RF-XX is skipped and the branch proceeds directly to
      XX-TS.
    rule: a branch's XX-TS validates only the post-RF (or post-CR, if RF
      skipped) implementation.
    notation: in chains and traces, write RF{scope=BE} etc.; the short
      key form RF-BE is the dictionary alias (bax workflow/step-keys.sdd).

  SCScopedSemantics (Phase 151):
    definition: SC is ONE stage. SC-DB, SC-BE, SC-API, SC-FE, SC-MD,
      SC-DC are the SAME stage executed with a `scope:` parameter naming
      the branch artifact under security validation.
    rule: scoped SC instances are NOT separate stages — no stage
      explosion; each instance runs immediately after that branch's own
      XX-TS passes, checking only that branch's surface.
    rule: a delivery branch is not complete until its scoped SC-XX has
      passed, in addition to CR-XX (see step-keys.sdd).
    rule: this scoped, per-branch SC is distinct from the aggregate QA
      gate, which runs after all branches' XX-TS/SC-XX are done.
    notation: in chains and traces, write SC{scope=BE} etc.; the short
      key form SC-BE would need to be added as a dictionary alias
      (bax workflow/step-keys.sdd) — currently not listed there.


Phase124StateMapping:
  Purpose:
    Maps the PHASE 124 10-state task lifecycle to SDLC/STLC stages.
    The task lifecycle is the runtime engine state; SDLC stages are the
    engineering disciplines executed within those states.

  StateToStageMap:
    DISCOVERING    -> AN          (Analyze: scope, requirements, constraints)
    PLANNING       -> AR, BDD     (Architect: design, boundaries; BDD: acceptance criteria)
    IMPLEMENTING   -> DB, BE, API, FE, MD, DC  (Engineering: database, backend, API, frontend, mobile, docs)
    TESTING        -> DB_TS, BE_TS, FE_TS, MD_TS, DC_TS, SC (scoped), QA  (per-layer test suites + scoped security + aggregate QA)
    FIXING         -> RF (scoped, post-CR change requests), or returns to TESTING (post-failure)  (Failure classification -> targeted fix/refactor -> retest)
    REVIEWING      -> ARCH, CR, BRU, CRU  (Architecture review, code review, business/quality gates)
    DOCUMENTING    -> D1          (Docs arm: human-readable documentation)
    LEARNING       -> Knowledge Gate  (Evaluate learning gate: NEW_KNOWLEDGE | EXISTING_UPDATED | ...)
    COMPLETED      -> VR          (Final verification and acceptance)
    BLOCKED        -> (suspended)  (External dependency or decision pending)
    ESCALATED      -> (human)     (Autonomy ceiling reached; human intervention required)

  SubStateTransitions:
    TESTING -> FAILED -> FIXING -> TESTING  (bounded by failure_budget and loop_score)
    IMPLEMENTING -> TESTING -> REVIEWING -> COMPLETED
    REVIEWING(CR change requests) -> FIXING(RF, scoped) -> TESTING(XX-TS, scoped) -> SC(scoped) -> REVIEWING/COMPLETED
    All states can -> BLOCKED (on dependency/decision stall)
    All states can -> ESCALATED (on autonomy ceiling breach)

  TaskLifecycleTrace:
    #01  DISCOVERING    -> Load task context (context-builder.sdd, memory-model.sdd)
    #02  PLANNING       -> Create plan, validate DAG (tasks.sdd, chains/graph.sdd)
    #03  IMPLEMENTING   -> Write code (project/ scaffold, stage outputs)
    #04  TESTING        -> Run tests (TEST-DISCOVERY-GATE, CHANGE-FILES-ONLY rule)
    #05  REVIEWING      -> Human gates (BRU, CRU, MANUAL-QA-GATE)
    #06  FIXING         -> Failure -> Classify -> Fix/Refactor (RF, scoped) -> Re-test (LOOP-PROTECTION)
    #07  DOCUMENTING    -> Generate docs/ (HUMAN-DOCS-GATE)
    #08  LEARNING       -> Knowledge gate (LEARNING-GATE, memory-consolidation.sdd)
    #09  COMPLETED      -> Done proof (DONE-PROOF.sdd, VR)
    #10  BLOCKED/ESCALATED -> Human notification (AUTONOMY-POLICY.sdd)

  Navigation:
    TaskStateMachine: @../tasks/TASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
    LoopProtection: @../tasks/LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd
    FailureClassification: @../tasks/FAILURE-CLASSIFICATION.sdd
    AutonomyPolicy: @../tasks/AUTONOMY-POLICY.sdd
    DoneProof: @../tasks/DONE-PROOF.sdd
    LearningGate: @../workflow/learning-gate.sdd
    HumanDocsGate: @../workflow/human-docs-gate.sdd
    ExecutionContract: @../tasks/EXECUTION-CONTRACT.sdd
    ExecutionLoop: @../workflow/execution-loop.sdd

State: +
   (extended with PHASE 124 10-state task lifecycle mapping to SDLC/STLC stages)
   (added sub-state transitions, task lifecycle trace, and cross-references)
   (Phase 151: unified branch pipeline XX -> CR-XX -> RF-XX -> XX-TS -> SC-XX;
    added RF stage + RFScopedSemantics, scoped SC + SCScopedSemantics;
    added missing DB_TS stage; fixed DC-TS -> DC_TS naming; filled
    StateToStageMap gaps (DC in IMPLEMENTING; DB_TS, DC_TS, SC in TESTING;
    RF in FIXING))
